Package: knowledge
Title: Fisheries Evidence and Tuned Habitat Thresholds for BC Watershed Groups
Version: 0.4.33
Date: 2026-11-06
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128",
                       affiliation = "New Graph Environment Ltd.")),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
    )
Description: Gathers fisheries evidence for British Columbia watershed
    groups (provincial fish sampling records, past reports, cited literature
    values with their quotes, intrinsic-potential models and life-history
    timing) and tunes from the fish records the gradient and stream-size
    thresholds that the link habitat models use: it places sampling visits
    on link's stream segments, scores candidate rules on held-out watershed
    groups, grades segments by expected use, and tabulates, maps and compares
    the tuned rules with link's defaults. It also pulls PSCIS crossing layers
    and past-report tables for a group and checks stream names before a
    search. Under active development.
